1. Corrections
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
First of all, I need to make two corrections to the "The Spoilers" section of 
Revision 8.00 of the Spoilers which has already been distributed. 

A) It has been pointed out to me that a new numbering system has been adopted 
for Nethack version 3.1.  Patches are denoted by adding a period and the 
patch number to 3.1 instead of a letter.  Letters infer a non-official patch.
Thus, the first paragraph should read as follows:

The information contained in this file is relevant to Nethack version 3.1.1 
(i.e. Nethack version 3.1, patch level 1), the most recent version of Nethack 
available at the time this file was posted.  Although much of the information 
contained within the Spoilers is also relevant to previous versions of 
Nethack, don't depend on it.  Our suggestion is that you get a copy of the 
latest and greatest version of Nethack - version 3.1.1. 

B) It has also been pointed out that there is no longer a HARD option.  I had 
assumed that it was still there (forgive me for not reading through all the 
.include files <GRIN>).  Thus, the second paragraph should read as follows:

Additionally, for the sake of simplicity we have assumed that all the compile 
options are at their default settings unless otherwise specified.  This means 
that all the optional code is compiled in, etc. 

